'''Uruava''' is an [[language death|extinct]] [[Austronesian languages|Austronesian language]] formerly spoken in southeast Bougainville, [[Papua New Guinea]].

The language was spoken around [[Arawa, Papua New Guinea|Arawa]]. It was recorded shortly before its speakers shifted to the non-Austronesian [[Nasioi language]].<ref>{{cite book|first=Matthew|last=Spriggs|editor-first1=Anthony|editor-last1=Regan|editor-first2=Helga-Maria|editor-last2=Griffin|chapter=Bougainville's early history: an archaeological perspective|year=2005|title=
Bougainville Before the Conflict|publisher=Stranger Journalism|isbn=9781740761383|page=17}}</ref>

